---
source: crates/rustman-cli/src/tests.rs
expression: help
---
Run the requests under files or folders and report the results

Usage: rustman run [OPTIONS] [PATH]...

Arguments:
  [PATH]...
          Request files or folders to run (default: the current directory)

Options:
      --env <NAME>
          Environment (default: RUSTMAN_ENV, then default_environment)

      --workspace <DIR>
          Workspace directory (default: search from the current directory upwards)

      --var <K=V>
          Set a variable, above every other source (repeatable): --var k=v

      --timeout <DURATION>
          Total timeout per request, replacing settings.timeout_ms: 500ms, 5s, 2m, or a number of milliseconds

  -k, --insecure
          Do not verify TLS certificates (exchanges are flagged insecure)

      --no-history
          Do not record the exchanges in history

      --bail
          Skip the remaining requests after the first failed or errored one

      --filter <FILTER>
          Run only matching requests: tag:<name>, or a glob over request ids such as 'users/*' (repeatable; a request matching any runs)

      --iterations <N>
          Run the selected requests this many times
          
          [default: 1]

      --parallel <N>
          Run up to N folders at once; requests in one folder stay in order unless its _collection.yaml sets parallel: true
          
          [default: 1]

      --reporter <FORMAT[:PATH]>
          Report format, optionally written to a file: pretty, json, junit or tap, as in json or junit:out/junit.xml (repeatable; default: pretty on stdout)

      --color <WHEN>
          Color: auto (a terminal without NO_COLOR or TERM=dumb), always or never
          
          [default: auto]

  -v, --verbose...
          Log more on stderr: -v requests, -vv headers, -vvv everything (RUST_LOG, when set, replaces these levels)

  -h, --help
          Print help
